# AYN Odin 3 patch series -- applied top-to-bottom, before the OGC block and
# before patches/local/. `#` lines and anything after a `#` are ignored.
#
# This is the Odin-3-relevant subset of armada's 158-line series. Armada carries
# every device it supports (SM8250 + SM8550 + SM8650 + SM8750); we only need the
# CQ8725S/SM8750 path plus the shared msm/qcom fixes.
#
# Every entry here is fetched verbatim from armada-packages at ARMADA_REF, with
# ROCKNIX as a fallback source. Nothing in this file is locally rebased -- if a
# patch ever needs local changes it moves to patches/local/ and gets an entry in
# the "Local divergence" section of docs/PATCHES.md.
#
# Provenance lives in docs/PATCHES.md. Keep them in sync: an unattributed patch
# is one nobody can rebase. Fetch with scripts/fetch-patches.sh.
# ============== SoC identification ==============
# CQ8725S is the Dragonwing part in the Odin 3. Mainline doesn't know the ID.
0026-dt-bindings-arm-qcom-ids-Add-SoC-ID-for-CQ8725S.patch
0027-soc-qcom-socinfo-Add-CQ8725S-SoC-ID.patch

# ============== SM8750 SoC DT enablement ==============
0033-arm64-dts-qcom-sm8750-gpu-clock-controllers.patch
0034-arm64-dts-qcom-sm8750-Add-UART15.patch
0035-arm64-dts-qcom-sm8750-set-CPU-capacity-dmips-mhz.patch
0037-arm64-dts-qcom-sm8750-add-CPU-thermal-cooling.patch
0038-arm64-dts-qcom-sm8750-add-GPU-nodes.patch
0038a-arm64-dts-qcom-sm8750-map-A8xx-RSCC-registers.patch
20260424_neil_armstrong_arm64_dts_qcom_sm8_456_50_add_missing_cx_power_domain_to_gcc.patch

# ============== GPU — Adreno 830 (A8xx) ==============
# Not in mainline. Without this there is no GPU at all.
#
# Load-bearing for userspace too: this declares ADRENO_CHIP_IDS(0x44050000), and
# ALARM's stock turnip has the DRM/msm form of exactly that id (0xffff44050000)
# but NOT the rev-0001 variants. So on this kernel stock Mesa is expected to
# work. If the id here ever moves to 0x44050001, turnip stops matching the GPU
# and packages/README.md ("Mesa: probably stock, decided by one chip-id") is the
# two-line fix.
0049-drm-msm-a8xx-add-adreno-830-catalog.patch
0050-clk-qcom-gxclkctl-kaanapali-fix-gx-gdsc-collapse.patch
0120-20250728_konradybcio_gpu_cc_power_requirements_reality_check.patch
0121-pmdomain-qcom-rpmhpd-presync-floor-gmu-rails.patch

# ============== Display / DRM ==============
0010-msm-resource-cleanup.patch
0048-drm-msm-dsi-reparent-byte-pixel-src-to-xo-on-disable.patch

# The Odin 3 panel is compatible = "chipone,icna3520" (see dts/), so 0028 is
# load-bearing: without it there is no display.
#
# 0028's Kconfig hunk needs both of its alphabetical neighbours present:
#   DRM_PANEL_BOE_XM91080G          above  -> NOT in 7.2-rc7, so 0056 is required
#   DRM_PANEL_CHIPWEALTH_CH13726A   below  -> already upstream in 7.2-rc7
# So 0056 stays purely as context (an unused tristate driver, ~nothing), and
# Armada's 0057 is dropped — see below.
0056_Xm-Plus-XM91080G-panel.patch
0028-drm-panel-Add-panel-driver-for-Chipone-ICNA35XX-base.patch

# DROPPED: 0057_DDIC-CH13726A-panel.patch
# Landed upstream. 7.2-rc7 ships drivers/gpu/drm/panel/panel-chipwealth-ch13726a.c;
# Armada still carries the older pre-upstream version as panel-ddic-ch13726a.c,
# which would install a duplicate driver for the same panel. Not our device
# anyway — we only ever wanted it as Kconfig context, and upstream provides that.

0505-msm_gem-lock-before-put_iova_spaces.patch

